  "worked_solution": "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- There is no smallest $y$-value.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-\\infty $ and $1,$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-\\infty <y<1,$ which can also be written as  $-\\infty <f(x)<1.$",
